    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0480" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg406"/>

                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">St Petersburg, Russia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 12, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I take the liberty of sending you some more
                    extracts from the journals of the day, translated by Mr. Curtin.</p>
                <p>Mr. Curtin and myself were invited by the Society of Merchants of St. Petersburg
                    to dine with them on the occasion of the anniversary of the coronation of the
                    Emperor, (the accession to the throne,) and the liberation of the serfs. We were
                    received with great enthusiasm, and both made honorary members for life. The
                    Invalide is the Russian official paper. Bancroft’s allusion to Russia is well
                    received here.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>







